; Surrogate pair \uD800\uDD67 should decode to U+10167 (𐅧).
; This exercises the fallback to_char overload with a supplementary plane character.
; On Windows with wchar_t (16-bit), this would truncate and produce "?" instead.
(if (= "𐅧" "\uD800\uDD67")
  :success
  (throw "Surrogate pair \\uD800\\uDD67 did not decode to U+10167"))
